Fix shared queue defaults and optional export flag in CanSNPer2

- CanSNPer2.find_snps: results/export_results/called_snps defaults changed from mutable lists to None, with a fresh multiprocessing Queue per call when not supplied; the real call path (find_snps_multiproc) always passes its own queues, so behaviour there is unchanged (#6)
- CanSNPer2.__init__: self.export now read with kwargs.get("export", False), so constructing the object without the optional flag no longer raises KeyError; same pattern already used for ParseXMFA (#51)
